The manifest lists only requested root-level safetensors weights and
configuration, tokenizer, license, and model-card assets. It excludes ONNX,
training artifacts, and alternate weight formats. Weight SHA256 values
are upstream LFS metadata, not local verification of weight downloads.
Small-file SHA256 values are supplied only when the exact reconstructed
bytes match the pinned upstream git blob SHA1 (MEAS); otherwise SHA256 is
unknown and the git blob SHA1 is supplied. Downloaded files must be checked
before use. Architecture values come from pinned config.json files (EXT);
head dimensions are explicitly marked as derived when not provided
(INFERENCE). Seven safetensors files across six models total 16,361,825,248 bytes
(INFERENCE: arithmetic sum of upstream sibling sizes), below a decimal
20,000,000,000-byte weight budget. Configuration and tokenizer files are
additional to this weight-only total. OLMo's two shards store F32 weights;
do not load the complete checkpoint at once.
